{
 "id": "2026-10-10-isaias-late-hurricane",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "The Atlantic waited until October for its first hurricane. Then it slammed into Florida."
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Isaias became a hurricane over the Gulf of Mexico on October 7th. NOAA data cited by CBS News show that is the latest first hurricane of an Atlantic season in 121 years. Usually, the first one forms in early to mid August."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "After briefly reaching Category 3, Isaias came ashore near Destin, Florida, on Friday night as a Category 2. Forecasters warned of up to 15 inches of rain across Alabama and Florida. ABC News reports at least 800,000 homes and businesses without power."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Why so late? Meteorologists point largely to a strong El Niño that developed over the summer. It tends to tear Atlantic storms apart with strong winds high above the ocean. Meanwhile, CBS notes, the Pacific has been unusually active."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Follow for the next update."
  }
 ],
